From bb758eb4d609f4a133c46f7a4a6399eb12b76626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:22:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] cuda : persistent multi-token layer-half kernels for
 the Qwen3.5/3.6 MoE MTP verify on sm_60

Extends GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGA=1 to batches of 2..6 tokens (the MTP verify pass) and to the gated delta net with
recurrent-state snapshots (n_rs_seq > 0), which the MTP server uses at every batch size.

p60-mega-t.cu: one cooperative launch per layer half, templated on the token count. Activations are fp16 in shared
memory (pre-permuted so weight words pair up as half2), products are HFMA2 with short half2 chains flushed to fp32.
The MoE half computes the union of the tokens' experts once per row and loops only over the tokens routed to it;
the expert-down phase is split across blocks by cost. The GDN half writes the K conv and recurrent-state snapshots
with llama.cpp's slot semantics. The matchers verify every snapshot copy (source offset, cache slot, stride) and
fall back to the normal path otherwise; single-token MoE keeps the fp32 kernel.

2x P100, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q4_K_XL, 8 prompts x 256 tokens, MTP n5 + draft vocab:
  greedy        122.0 -> 157.6 t/s (+29%)
  prod sampler  116.1 -> 151.1 t/s (+30%), acceptance unchanged
Not bit-exact: wikitext KLD vs the stock ub=1 base at -ub 6 is 0.00430 (stock -ub 6: 0.00390), PPL 6.6118 vs
6.6112, same gap as the single-token path.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
